WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.000
Apparently, Sony's Morbius will be a very
specific kind of vampire — the sexy kind.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.220
"Very dashing."

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:14.680
Actor Jared Leto shared what appears to be
a set photo from the forthcoming flick to

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:19.091
his Instagram recently, and if you can look
past the rippling torso and tight abs, you

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.900
may find there's more going on than meets
the eye.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.779
The actor has been all about teasing Morbius
via social media: On April 4th, 2019, he even

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:32.730
posted a short video of himself in character,
standing on a busy city street while throngs

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.140
of passersby rush around him in a blur.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.920
Leto claimed to have posted the set photo
in honor of the anniversary of This is War,

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.920
the third album by his rock band 30 Seconds
to Mars.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.260
But it's obviously meant to be a bit of a
Morbius tease as well…

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:49.350
See that dark smear of blood at the corner
of Leto's mouth?

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.260
So, to state the obvious: Jared Leto is a
good-looking man, and he's obviously following

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:58.470
in the time-honored tradition of superhero
movie stars like Thor's Chris Hemsworth by

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:03.390
getting into incredible shape for his role
as Dr. Michael Morbius, the biochemist who

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.040
has traditionally been the staunch opponent
of your friendly neighborhood Spider-Man.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:11.280
But there are a couple of possible clues in
the photo that warrant a closer look.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:16.420
First, Leto is sporting a distinctive Casio
digital wristwatch... the kind that was popular

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.920
in the eighties and nineties.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.040
This could be a clue about the time period
Morbius will be set in.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:26.420
So far, director Daniel Espinosa hasn't revealed
any real plot details or the film's period

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.940
setting, but the watch's placement here certainly
invites speculation.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.000
Of course, it could just be indicative of
Leto's taste in timepieces.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:34.740
Difficult to say.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:39.200
More importantly: Either Leto has suddenly
sprouted a whole bunch of moles on his face,

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.080
or he's covered in those tracking dots used
in motion-capture performances.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:49.040
Note that in his vampire form, Morbius is,
well… frankly, he's hideous in the comics.

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:53.920
Rather than practical makeup, it appears that
special effects house Nvizage will be using

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.880
CGI to create the Living Vampire's ghastly
look.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:02:00.720
And yes, that's the same house that provided
the effects for Sony's Venom.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.880
"We are Venom."

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:11.380
This could be viewed as a positive or a negative,
depending on how you feel about Venom's special

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:11.880
effects.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:16.300
While plenty of fans were perfectly satisfied
with the title character's appearance, others

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.140
felt that the CGI left a lot to be desired.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.980
Some moviegoers even thought the effects looked
dated.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.610
Of course, Venom and Morbius are two characters
with completely different looks, and even

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:30.870
if Nvizage fell short in rendering the former,
they could still totally crush it when it

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:31.980
comes to Morbius.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.700
After all, the special effects house did awesome
work for Espinosa on his film Life and on

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:40.040
last year's underrated Nazi zombie thriller
Overlord.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:46.420
Plus, it's worth noting that Venom made 855
million dollars worldwide, which may encourage

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:50.320
Sony to pony up a bit more cash for Morbius'
special effects budget.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.320
At any rate, Leto's excitement over the upcoming
film is positively contagious, and we're psyched

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.360
to see what spin he puts on the material.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.820
Following Venom, Morbius will be the second
installment in the Sony Universe of Marvel

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:06.180
Characters, which the studio is building because
it still holds the rights to a whole bunch

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:08.500
of characters associated with Spider-Man.

00:03:08.709 --> 00:03:13.300
The Sony and Marvel deal won't last forever,
and Sony's leverage with Marvel could depend

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:17.380
on how well its Sony Universe of Marvel offerings
do at the box office.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.000
As previously noted, Venom did just fine.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.030
We'll see just how big of a bargaining chip
Morbius represents when it hits the big screen

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.860
on July 31st, 2020.

